  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Friday)\nIssued at 949 PM CST FRI NOV 13 2026\n\nWinds are still expected to decouple overnight, allowing for\nradiational cooling to occur over a good portion of the state.\nBecause of that, overnight lows are expected to fall near, or\nbelow freezing in many locations, with a Freeze Warning going\ninto effect at Midnight, and remaining in effect until 8 AM\nSaturday. The same thing is expected to occur again Saturday\nnight, with another Freeze warning in effect for that same\ntimeframe. Thankfully, overnight lows should stay slightly more\ninsulated Sunday night, as clouds return to the skies during the\novernight hours.\n\nThese clouds will be associated with a weak upper-level low that\nforms off to our west, moving into the region sometime on Monday.\nWhile this low pressure will provide ample lift for increased\nrain chances, a lack of moisture return ahead of this low should \nkeep any form of precipitation limited. Upper-level ridging is \nstill expected to build in across the SE closer to the middle of \nthe workweek, with afternoon highs climbing back into the \nupper-60s and mid-70s by Thursday. With that being said, \nconfidence is high that overnight lows will stay on the cool side,\nas cold air remains filtering down the Appalachian Mountains. \nOtherwise, rainfall remains absent from the forecast for most of \nthe next seven days.\n\n/44/",
